Author: funding <wyx20021207@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 30 20:55:13 2026 +0800

    fix(agent): report the system prompt before a session's first message (#974)
    
    * fix(agent): report the system prompt before a session's first message
    
    `get_state` read `agent.state.systemPrompt`, which Pi 0.86 turned into a
    getter that replays the transcript. A session that has not run anything
    yet has no system message to replay, so the field came back as "" and the
    System panel rendered its "prompt is empty (tools are disabled)" state for
    every brand-new session.
    
    Read the session-level getter instead. It renders the prompt from the
    current options, which are populated while the session is built, so it is
    already correct before the first run; its meaning did not change in 0.86,
    and it is what the old `_baseSystemPrompt` field held.
    
    Fixes #973
    
    * fix(agent): keep the replayed system prompt once a run has recorded one
    
    The session getter renders the prompt from the base options, so after a run it
    drops the sections a before_agent_start handler changed for that run. Report the
    transcript replay when it has a prompt and fall back to the getter only while it
    is still empty.
    
